   "selected_by": "CALLER, against the `auto` rule, on an out-of-fold VALIDATION diagnostic \u2014 not on the sealed test. `auto` ranks maps by out-of-fold ECE and picks plain `isotonic` (2.96% vs isotonic_pav 5.45% vs platt 8.09%); both isotonic maps also pass the E21 <=5% gate on the sealed test (4.22% / 4.60%). The override rests on the merge END, which is the only region T_hi cuts: the same out-of-fold pass reports isotonic's merge-end AUC at 41.2% (BELOW CHANCE, n 103) against isotonic_pav's 70.3%, because isotonic-over-bins compresses every merge-end pair into one top bin. Measured consequence: under isotonic the shipped `model|cross` cut and the dev search's own answer differ by 1.5e-8 and merge different sets, so a threshold there is a rank cut spelled as a probability. The choice is DECISION-NEUTRAL on this cohort \u2014 isotonic, isotonic_pav and platt all produce the identical 3,166 / 6,510 / 33,499 zones, the identical 449-pair judged merge set and the identical zone recall (scratchpad/w4g/eval_auto vs eval_pav) \u2014 so nothing but expressibility and the store floor turns on it.",
